		{
			dependencies: [
				"668FDEE4E8F291B5"
				"125A9DB351593D71"
			]
			id: "25EA4D1276CD3475"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "26E8862270BAD4DD"
					item: {
						Count: 1
						ForgeCaps: {
							"celestisynth:celestisynthitemstackcapabilities": {
								cs.aquaSkin: 0
							}
						}
						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						tag: {
							author: "Mr6trt"
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"Before time had a name… before even the stars were sure of their place in the night… there was Cadrixka.\\n\\nNot a man. Not quite a god. Something between.\\n\\nThey called him the Architect of Scrolls, the Weaver of Laws.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He did not learn magic — he commanded it.\\n\\nWhere others studied flame, he bent it into spirals.\\nWhere others tamed water, he whispered it into memory. No spell was beyond him. No ritual unsolvable.\\n\\nBut genius births vanity.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"And Cadrixka — undying, untouched by age — began to ask the question no mage dared utter aloud:\\n\\nWhat lies beyond this world?\\n\\nNot just the stars. Not death. Beyond death.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He called it The Otherverse.\\nA realm of thoughts that think themselves. A world not made of matter… but of intention.\\nThere, he believed, true creation awaited.Not borrowed spells, not conjured flames real summoning.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Creatures never seen. Laws never written.\\n\\nGodhood earned.\\n\\nBut even gods pay a price.\\n\\nThe Watchers of the Otherverse answered him.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Not in voice. In dream.\\n\\nIn return for knowledge, they asked for what even Cadrixka had long kept hidden:\\n\\nHis immortality.\\n\\nA curse, to some. But to him power.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"And he gave it up. Willingly.\\n\\nWith the last years of his life ticking away like falling sand, he created. Feverishly. Madly.\\nA staff, unlike any spell-forged rod. A conduit, not of power… but of calling.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He named it after himself — because who else could deserve that honor?\\nCadrixka, the Summoning Staff.\\nIt was not buried. It was hidden. Its reappearance would not be found in scrolls.\\nIts trail would not be left in maps.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"But in whispers. In death. In shadow.\\n\\n“Let it be earned,” Cadrixka wrote in his final tome, now lost to time.\\n“Let them prove worthy — not with brilliance, but with obsession.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The trial of the Summoner is this:\\n\\nWhen one has silenced the lost echoes of two hundred and fifty wandering spirits…\\n\\nWhen they have gathered the final breath of all mortal beasts, each one known beneath the sun…\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"When they have stood with sand of souls stacked like towers, one thousand strong…\\n\\nWhen every branch of magic — from the simplest spark to the deepest curse — has passed through their hands…\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"And when they face the devourer of time — the one that writhes in void — and do not flee…\\nThen shall the gates open.\\nThen shall the pact be offered again. And then, the staff shall rise.\\n\\nBut beware.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"It does not answer to you.\\n\\nThe staff remembers. It watches.\\nIt listens to the Otherverse, still.\\n\\nThose who wield it may summon beasts that have no name… cast powers no scroll has ever scribed.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"But to summon… is to invite.\\n\\nAnd not all invitations are declined.\\n\\nCadrixka lives on.\\n\\nNot in flesh. Not in spirit.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"But in every crackle of the staff’s black core…\\nIn every step closer to the summoner’s doom.\\n\\nPower is a circle. And Cadrixka drew it perfectly.\"}"
							]
							title: "Cadrixca Omega"
						}
					}
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "5F96A64A9F73F73A"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 250
				}
